... The word (aidv) here used, and the equivalent term ... commonly translated world, are so frequently used for the mass of mankind, considered in opposition to the people of God, that there can be no good reason for departing from the common interpretation, especially as the sense which it affords is so good in itself and so well suited to the context.

By the renewing of your mind. This phrase is intended to be explanatory of the preceding. The transformation to which Christians are exhorted, is not a mere external change, but one which results from a change of heart, an entire alteration of the state of the mind. The word rendered mind is used, as it is here, frequently in the New Testament, Rom. 1;

28. Eph. 4: 17, 23. Col. 2: 18, &c., in all these and in similar cases it does not differ from the word heart.
